     A* FLROUTP - work order routing: one row per operation.  (GJA-917)
     A*
     A* Routed standard hours are the only real input to a capacity
     A* plan, so a work order with no rows here is invisible to the
     A* schedule - which the data-confidence scan reports.
     A*
     A                                      UNIQUE
     A          R FLROUTR                   TEXT('Work order routing step')
     A            FLRWO          8P 0       COLHDG('Work' 'Order')
     A                                      TEXT('Work order number')
     A            FLRSEQ         3P 0       COLHDG('Op' 'Seq')
     A                                      TEXT('Operation sequence')
     A            FLRWCTR        6A         COLHDG('Work' 'Centre')
     A                                      TEXT('Work centre code')
     A            FLRDESC       40A         COLHDG('Operation')
     A                                      TEXT('Operation description')
     A            FLRSTHR        5P 1       COLHDG('Std' 'Hours')
     A                                      TEXT('Standard hours')
     A            FLRACHR        5P 1       COLHDG('Actual' 'Hours')
     A                                      TEXT('Actual hours reported')
     A            FLRSTAT        1A         COLHDG('Sts')
     A                                      TEXT('W/R/C/H operation status')
     A            FLRSTRT        8S 0       COLHDG('Started')
     A                                      TEXT('Started YYYYMMDD')
     A            FLRCOMP        8S 0       COLHDG('Completed')
     A                                      TEXT('Completed YYYYMMDD')
     A          K FLRWO
     A          K FLRSEQ
